# 13. PROMISCUOUS MODE

A network interface normally processes traffic intended for it.

**Promiscuous mode** allows the interface to pass more Ethernet frames to the capture software for inspection.

Important:

> Promiscuous mode does **not** magically allow you to see all traffic on a switched network.

Modern switched networks normally deliver unicast traffic only to the relevant port.

---

# 14. SWITCHED NETWORK

Consider:

```text
PC-A ──┐
PC-B ──┼── Switch
PC-C ──┘
```

If PC-A communicates directly with PC-B, PC-C normally cannot simply capture all of that unicast traffic.

Therefore:

> Wireshark on an ordinary switched endpoint does not automatically reveal everybody else's traffic.

