# 39. TCP STREAM

Wireshark can reconstruct packets belonging to a TCP conversation.

Right-click a TCP packet and use:

> **Follow → TCP Stream**

This is extremely useful for analyzing a conversation in an authorized PCAP.

---

# 40. HTTP STREAM

For supported HTTP traffic, you can similarly use:

> **Follow → HTTP Stream**

This helps reconstruct the application conversation.

---

# 41. WHY FOLLOW STREAM IS USEFUL

Instead of examining:

```text
Packet 10
Packet 14
Packet 17
Packet 21
Packet 25
...
```

Wireshark can reconstruct the conversation:

```text
Client → Request
Server → Response
Client → Request
Server → Response
```

This makes analysis much easier.

---

# 42. TCP STREAM INDEX

Wireshark can identify different TCP conversations using stream identifiers.

A display filter such as:

```text
tcp.stream == 0
```

shows packets belonging to a particular TCP stream.

Example:

```text
tcp.stream == 5
```

selects stream 5.

