# ⭐ ONE-LINE EXAM ANSWER

> **Wireshark is a network protocol analyzer used to capture and inspect packets, allowing analysts to investigate protocols, hosts, connections, and suspicious network behavior; however, encryption such as TLS can prevent captured application data from being directly read.**

# 🏆 DAY 32 GOLDEN RULE

> **Don't analyze packets one by one without context. First identify the hosts and protocols, then filter, reconstruct conversations, correlate timestamps, validate the evidence, and report the finding.**